  "id": "anticipation",
  "term": "anticipation",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, anticipation means either a mental state of readiness for something expected to happen, or a voluntary response made before the stimulus actually appears. The term can thus refer both to expectant awareness and to an early reaction observed before an event.",
